p>Tip (Detailed Explanation):</p>
<p>a) Recursive Approach:</p>
<ol>
<li data-length=3D"1">check whether the root is null or not..</li>
<li data-length=3D"1">go to the left most node of tree using RECURSION and =
store node.</li>
<li data-length=3D"1">go to the right most node of tree using RECURSION and=
 store node.</li>
<li data-length=3D"1">swap both stored node.</li>
<li data-length=3D"1">return root</li>
</ol>
<p>-- Time Complexity: O(n)<br>
-- Space Complexity: O(n)</p>
<p>b) Iterative Approach:</p>
<ol>
<li data-length=3D"1">create Queue</li>
<li data-length=3D"1">check whether the root is null or not.</li>
<li data-length=3D"1">add root to the queue.</li>
<li data-length=3D"1">loop until queue is not empty and then remove element=
 from queue and store it. Then, check for left and right element and add to=
 queue.<br>
Finally, swap the element.</li>
<li data-length=3D"1">return root.</li>
</ol>
<p>-- Time Complexity: O(n)<br>
-- Space Complexity: O(n)</p></div><span style=3D"font-size: 0px; line-heig=
